# LED Vision Lab — Agent Rules

## Source of Truth
Before any implementation, read `Goal.md`, `Roadmap.md`, `Architecture.md`, and `AI Agent Instructions.md`.

## Discuss Before Implementing
**Always propose and discuss a plan with the user before writing code.**
Get explicit approval before starting implementation of any phase or feature.

## One Phase at a Time
Work only on the current Roadmap phase. Do not implement future phases unless explicitly requested.

## Architecture Must Be Respected
- All detectors implement the common `LedDetector` interface
- No CV logic in API routes or frontend
- No training logic in inference code
- Dataset generation, detection, training, API, and web UI stay separated

## Python Standards
- Type hints everywhere
- `pathlib` for all filesystem paths
- Dataclasses for structured data (`DetectionResult`, configs)
- Explicit error handling — never silently swallow exceptions
- Small functions with one clear responsibility

## Configuration Over Hard-Coding
HSV thresholds, image dimensions, model paths, seeds, dataset size — all go in config files, not in source code.

## Dataset & Model Artifacts
- Do NOT commit generated datasets or trained model files to Git
- Generator code + configs + small samples only
- All training must be reproducible via a random seed

## Testing
Every feature needs tests before it is "done":
1. Run relevant tests
2. Confirm existing tests still pass
3. Report what was tested

## Git Commits
Use conventional commits:
```
feat(hsv): implement LED state detection
fix(api): reject invalid image uploads
test(knn): add feature extractor unit tests
docs(dataset): document metadata schema
```

## Definition of Done
- Requested behavior works
- Follows architecture
- Tests exist and pass
- Error cases handled
- Docs updated if needed
- No unrelated changes introduced
